load-hang.patch (2026-11-05, branch fix/load-hang): toolkit changes on top of the toolkit patch of main 0cdea24.

GCM_STALL_GAP_MS (live, default 100; 0 = wall time as before; toggle after PS3T_ENG_SHADE_BACKFACE):
the FIFO walker's two wall-clock bounds -- the self-JUMP park grace (GCM_PARK_GRACE_MS, 1000 in the
port's run.sh) and the bounded semaphore acquire (GCM_SEMA_ACQUIRE_MS, 200) -- count only time the
walker saw pass in steps of at most that many ms. A longer gap between two checks of the same wait
means the process stood still (starved Mac, paging, SIGSTOP); it is not counted and is logged once
("<n> ms with no drain pass (process stalled?) not counted against a park/acquire bound"). Before,
a stall of 1 s or more inside a park "expired" it: the jump-park resync dropped the rest of the
frame (only the ref fences are rescued), which is the state the 2026-10-23 city-load hangs were
left in (get on the ring JUMP at put, park_off 0, label 135 at 0).

Diagnostics in the "ref stuck" report: the flip state (status, request/tick sequence, request
count, undelivered vblank/flip handler bits) and PS3_HANG_PEEK=<ea>:<len>[,...] (hex) guest words.


